# Migrating On-Prem SQL Server to SQL Server on Azure VM Using Backup to URL (Azure Blob Storage)

Migrating your on-premises SQL Server to a SQL Server VM in Azure gives you full control over the SQL Server engine while benefiting from cloud scalability, security, and simplified infrastructure management. The primary method in this guide uses SQL Server's native **BACKUP/RESTORE ... TO/FROM URL** syntax, authenticated with a SQL Server credential created directly from the **storage account** (using the storage account key), so the on-prem instance streams the backup straight to Azure Blob Storage over HTTPS with no local `.bak` file and no intermediate file share.

An alternative that stages backups through an Azure Files (CIFS/SMB) share first is also included further down, for teams that prefer to keep an SMB-based backup workflow.

